      "title": "Read me: models and links",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Alien Delivery - RIFE x2 smoothing (24 -> 48 fps)\nThe smoothing step: RIFE 4.26 doubles the frames of one upscaled shot (2560x1440, 24 fps -> 48 fps) and keeps its sound. Run it **per shot**, before joining shots: across a hard cut RIFE draws a ghost frame.\n\nThe film's upscaled shot D1 is in `inputs/alien_delivery_D1_2560_24fps.mp4`: copy it into `ComfyUI/input` and queue. For your own clip, pick it in Load Video; the output fps must be twice the source (48 for 24 fps clips).\n\n## Models\n- **RIFE 4.26 frame interpolation** (0.02 GB)  \n  file `rife_v4.26.safetensors` -> put in `ComfyUI/models/frame_interpolation/`  \n  https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Frame-Interpolation/resolve/main/frame_interpolation/rife_v4.26.safetensors\n\n## Custom nodes\nNone - Frame Interpolation and the video nodes are built into ComfyUI 0.44.\n\n## Measured on the RTX 3080\nAbout 55-60 s per 6.6 s shot at 2560x1440 (the app ran it in two chunks of ~78 frames to keep RAM low; one pass of a whole shot needs about 30 GB of RAM at 2560).\n\n## How the film was made\n1. **Frames** - every shot opens on a still drawn with Codex image generation (1672x941, cropped to 1632x928). One master view per scene; close shots are crops of it, re-detailed.\n2. **Shots** - this H3 + Pika workflow, 6 s each (158 frames, 24 fps), opening frame, or first + last frame where both frames share one locked camera.\n3. **Upscale** - NVIDIA RTX Video Super Resolution to 2560x1440 (NVIDIA Visual Enhancer `VE_CLI.exe`, outside ComfyUI). It must run on the 24 fps original, before smoothing.\n4. **Smoothing** - the RIFE x2 workflow, per shot (never across a cut, RIFE makes a ghost frame at hard cuts) -> 48 fps.\n5. **Music** - Google Lyria 3.5 (instrumental, \"retro sci-fi comedy space funk, 112 BPM\"), mixed ~14 LU under the dialogue with sidechain ducking in FFmpeg.\n\nMachine: RTX 3080 10 GB, 64 GB RAM, ComfyUI 0.44.0, PyTorch 2.11 + CUDA 13.0."
      ],
